<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Bush returns twelve days after starting methimazole 20 mg daily, on metoprolol succinate 50 mg daily and apixaban 5 mg twice daily since his hospital stay. He has had no palpitations or irregular pulse on his home monitor and feels well. He has walked daily but has not run yet, as advised. He has had no fever, sore throat, mouth ulcers, rash, itching, yellow eyes, or dark urine on methimazole, and no bleeding or bruising on apixaban. He takes every dose. He has no eye pain, grittiness, or double vision. He saw the endocrinologist this morning, and radioactive iodine is planned for next week. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rhythm</td><td>No palpitations; regular pulse on home checks</td></tr><tr><td>Thyrotoxic symptoms</td><td>Feels well; still a little heat-intolerant</td></tr><tr><td>Methimazole safety</td><td>No fever, sore throat, rash, jaundice, or dark urine</td></tr><tr><td>Apixaban safety</td><td>No bleeding or bruising; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Activity</td><td>Daily walks; not yet running</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

