    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Graves&apos; disease with hyperthyroidism, improving on methimazole (E05.00)</content>. Free T4 2.2 ng/dL, down from 3.6, and total T3 176 ng/dL, now in range; TSH still suppressed at 0.01, as expected. Neutrophil count 3.5 x10³/µL and ALT 30 U/L are normal on methimazole. The endocrinologist confirms Graves&apos; disease without eye disease and recommends radioactive iodine. [S]<list><item>Stop methimazole three days before radioactive iodine, which is booked for next week.</item><item>Radiation-safety instructions given in writing by the endocrinology clinic.</item><item>Free T4 and total T3 six to seven weeks after the treatment.</item><item>Expect hypothyroidism within weeks to months; levothyroxine when it comes.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Paroxysmal atrial fibrillation, in sinus rhythm (I48.0)</content>. Sinus rhythm at 72 per minute on metoprolol, with no recurrence since discharge. CHA2DS2-VASc 1 and HAS-BLED 1; apixaban continues while he is thyrotoxic, as agreed at intake. [S]<list><item>Continue metoprolol succinate 50 mg daily and apixaban 5 mg twice daily.</item><item>Gentle running can resume in two weeks if his pulse stays regular.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Heart rate and rhythm</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>72 per minute, regular; no recurrence of atrial fibrillation since discharge</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Every visit; target below 130/80</td><td>Completed today</td><td>132/70 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>86.4 kg, BMI 24.4</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Atrial fibrillation symptoms</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>12-lead ECG or rhythm strip</td><td>When rhythm assessment is indicated or symptoms change</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Pulse regular on examination and on home checks; intake ECG in sinus rhythm</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Transthoracic echocardiogram</td><td>At diagnosis; repeat with clinical change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal structure, left atrial size, and ejection fraction in hospital</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>CHA2DS2-VASc and HAS-BLED</td><td>Yearly and with any change in clinical status</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Scored at intake: CHA2DS2-VASc 1 (age 65 to 74), HAS-BLED 1 (age over 65)</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Anticoagulant adherence and bleeding</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses; no bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Creatinine and eGFR on apixaban</td><td>At baseline and at least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Creatinine 0.92 mg/dL, eGFR 87 at intake; full dose is correct</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin on anticoagulation</td><td>At least yearly; sooner with symptoms</td><td>Up to date</td><td>14.8 g/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Alcohol, tobacco, and physical activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No alcohol since the hospital stay; never used tobacco; daily walks, running to resume in steps</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Sleep apnea symptom screen</td><td>At diagnosis and at least yearly</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not asked at intake or today. Deviation: the screen due at diagnosis was missed; it is added to the next visit&apos;s checklist</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Free T4 and total T3 on methimazole</td><td>Two to six weeks after starting, then every four to eight weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Free T4 2.2 ng/dL, total T3 176 ng/dL, TSH 0.01 mIU/L</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>White cell count with differential and liver tests on methimazole</td><td>At baseline; then with fever, sore throat, jaundice, or other symptoms</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Checked before radioactive iodine at the consultant&apos;s request: neutrophils 3.5 x10³/µL, ALT 30 U/L</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Methimazole side effects</td><td>Every visit while on methimazole</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None; written warning about fever and sore throat repeated</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Eye assessment for Graves&apos; orbitopathy</td><td>At diagnosis and before radioactive iodine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No orbitopathy; never smoker, so no steroid cover is needed</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Endocrinology consultation</td><td>At diagnosis of Graves&apos; disease, to choose definitive treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today; radioactive iodine chosen</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Resting heart rate below 110 per minute without palpitations while thyrotoxic. Outcome by 1991-05-20: Heart rate 72 in sinus rhythm on metoprolol two weeks after intake [S]</item><item>No atrial fibrillation once no longer thyrotoxic, confirmed by ambulatory monitoring before the anticoagulation decision. In progress; target 1991-09-11 [S]</item><item>TSH within 0.4 to 4.0 mIU/L on levothyroxine. In progress; target 1991-10-16 [S]</item><item>Back to running three miles several days a week without symptoms. In progress; target 1991-09-11 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2023 ACC/AHA/ACCP/HRS Guideline for the Diagnosis and Management of Atrial Fibrillation (2023); 2016 American Thyroid Association Guidelines for Diagnosis and Management of Hyperthyroidism and Other Causes of Thyrotoxicosis (2016); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, atrial fibrillation and hypothyroidism monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Radioactive iodine next week. Review with thyroid tests in about seven weeks,